NAME
     mkimage - make a file system image from a directory

SYNOPSIS
     mkimage [-b BLOCKS] [-j BLOCKS] [-L LABEL] IMAGE DIR

DESCRIPTION
     mkimage writes an ext4 image holding what is under DIR, which is how
     a guest's or a container's root file system is made without a loop
     device or a mount.

OPTIONS
     -b BLOCKS   how big, in blocks of 4096 bytes
     -j BLOCKS   the journal's size
     -L LABEL    the volume label

SEE ALSO
     mkfs_ext4(8), losetup(8), vmm(1)
